{"name":"Wild River","hex":"#447382","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wild river","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A river system protected by government legislation requiring it to be maintained in its natural state."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wild_river"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wild river","blocks":[{"text":"A wild river or heritage river (Canada) is a river or a river system designated by a government to be protected and kept \"relatively untouched by development and are therefore in near natural condition, with all, or almost all, of its natural values intact.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Franklin_River_Tasmania.jpg/330px-Franklin_River_Tasmania.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_river"},{"title":"Wild River (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Wild River is a 1960 American drama film directed by Elia Kazan, and starring Montgomery Clift, Lee Remick, and Jo Van Fleet. It was filmed in the Tennessee Valley, and was adapted by Paul Osborn from two novels: Borden Deal's Dunbar's Cove and William Bradford Huie's Mud on the Stars, drawing for plot from Deal's story of a battle of wills between the nascent Tennessee Valley Authority and generations-old land owners, and from Huie's study of a rural Southern matriarchal family for characters and their reaction to destruction of their land, and the controversial employment methods of African-American laborers by the TVA. It marked Bruce Dern's film debut. In 2002, The film was selected for preservation in the National Film Registry by the Library of Congress."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Wild_River_%281960_film_poster_-_one_sheet%29.jpg/330px-Wild_River_%281960_film_poster_-_one_sheet%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_River_(film)"},{"title":"River","blocks":[{"text":"A river is a natural stream of fresh water that flows on land or inside caves towards another body of water at a lower elevation, such as an ocean, lake, or another river. A river may run dry before reaching the end of its course if it runs out of water, or only flow during certain seasons. Rivers are regulated by the water cycle, the processes by which water moves around the Earth. Water first enters rivers through precipitation, whether from rainfall, the runoff of water down a slope, the melting of glaciers or snow, or seepage from aquifers beneath the surface of the Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg/330px-Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Colo_river_valley.jpg/500px-Colo_river_valley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Colo_river_valley.jpg/1280px-Colo_river_valley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Colo_river_valley.jpg/500px-Colo_river_valley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View down Colo River Valley, New South Wales, being river recently protected as a Wild River under New South Wales' National Parks and Wildlife Act 1974","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColo_river_valley.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/2007.05.23_09_Recollet_Falls_French_River_Ontario.jpg/500px-2007.05.23_09_Recollet_Falls_French_River_Ontario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/2007.05.23_09_Recollet_Falls_French_River_Ontario.jpg/1280px-2007.05.23_09_Recollet_Falls_French_River_Ontario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/2007.05.23_09_Recollet_Falls_French_River_Ontario.jpg/500px-2007.05.23_09_Recollet_Falls_French_River_Ontario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View of French River, Canada's first designated Heritage River","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2007.05.23_09_Recollet_Falls_French_River_Ontario.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Lake_Manapouri_and_the_Monument.JPG/500px-Lake_Manapouri_and_the_Monument.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Lake_Manapouri_and_the_Monument.JPG/1280px-Lake_Manapouri_and_the_Monument.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Lake_Manapouri_and_the_Monument.JPG/500px-Lake_Manapouri_and_the_Monument.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View of Lake Manapouri, the protection of which was a key milestone in New Zealand environmental protection","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALake_Manapouri_and_the_Monument.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/USA_Big_Bend_Rio_Grande_TX.jpg/500px-USA_Big_Bend_Rio_Grande_TX.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/USA_Big_Bend_Rio_Grande_TX.jpg/1280px-USA_Big_Bend_Rio_Grande_TX.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com